# ─── Reference repositories (external) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Third-party / client source trees. NEVER publish. Both the directory form and
# the glob are kept deliberately: this is the highest-consequence rule in this
# file, and a single-pattern typo would expose proprietary code into a public
# repo irreversibly.
docs/.reference/
docs/.reference/**

# ─── docs/ is INTERNAL BY DEFAULT ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fail-closed. Everything under docs/ is ignored unless explicitly re-included
# in the allowlist below, so a new internal note dropped into docs/ can never
# become publishable by accident.
#
# To publish a doc: add an explicit `!docs/<name>` line — and read the file for
# host specifics (IPs, the live box's topology, credentials) BEFORE you do.
docs/*

# Internal implementation plans — never published. Both spellings are listed:
# `docs/plan/` (singular) exists on disk and is NOT matched by `docs/plans/**`.
docs/plan/
docs/plan/**
docs/plans/
docs/plans/**

# Public docs — explicit allowlist.
!docs/ACCESS-GATE.md
!docs/AGENT-DEPLOY.md
!docs/CLEAN-CODE-GUIDELINES.md
!docs/GIT-BRANCHING-MODEL.md
!docs/GIT-REDEPLOY-AND-CUSTOM-DOMAINS.md
!docs/HETZNER-DEPLOY.md
!docs/HTTPS-SETUP.md
!docs/LOCAL-TESTING.md
!docs/MAIL.md
!docs/VERSION-ROADMAP.md
# docs/specs and docs/examples publish by FILE TYPE, not wholesale. A bare
# `!docs/specs/` would re-include the entire subtree, making it opt-OUT — so an
# internal note dropped in there would be publishable, defeating the scheme.
#
# The dance below is required by a gitignore rule: a file cannot be re-included
# if a parent DIRECTORY is excluded, because git never descends into it. So
# re-include the directory, re-exclude its contents, re-include subdirectories
# so git keeps descending, then re-include the file types we actually publish.
!docs/examples/
docs/examples/**
!docs/examples/**/
!docs/examples/**/*.example

# docs/specs is INTERNAL. The PRD/TASKS/specification set is planning material
# written for one maintainer: statuses were never maintained (shipped features
# read "Not Started", deleted code reads "In Progress"), and the 4,940-line
# DROP-PAAS-SPECIFICATION.md presents SQLite, a drop.db platform store,
# Prometheus and built-in clustering as the shipped architecture -- none of
# which exist. Published, it would misinform every reader.
#
# FEATURE-INDEX.md is the one exception: rewritten as a standalone, accurate
# feature list that links to nothing under here.
!docs/specs/
docs/specs/**
!docs/specs/FEATURE-INDEX.md

drop-test/**

